  "body": "## What changed\n\nWith two setups holding the part differently, the viewport drew the other setup's WCS triad at its raw stored pose. That pose is in **its own** setup's frame, while the viewport shows the active setup's frame (`setup_align::view_pose`), so the triad landed off the part, e.g. at the stock's far corner in the report.\n\n- **New `setup_relative::wcs_view_pose(world, wcs_name, stored)` (app):** a WCS owned by a setup other than the active one is mapped through `transform_between(owner, active)`, the same rigid transform the part goes through. It then stays on the same spot of the part. The active setup's own WCS, and a document without setups, return `Ok(None)` and draw the stored pose unchanged.\n- **`interact::gizmos` (ui):** draws that pose. A refused transform hides the triad (logged at debug in app), so it is never drawn somewhere wrong. The UI makes no world-level calls, keeping to the layering law.\n\nThis is display only. Picking, `MoveModel`, stock transforms and the posted output are untouched. Decision record: `docs/decisions/558-other-setup-wcs.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New `crates/app/tests/wcs_view_pose.rs`, 3/3:**\n  - `another_setups_wcs_stays_on_its_spot_of_the_part`: TurnZ90, FlipX and TurnZ180 each land on the turned corner, not the stored place.\n  - `the_active_setups_own_wcs_and_a_setupless_document_draw_as_stored`\n  - `switching_the_shown_setup_keeps_the_wcs_on_the_part`\n- **New `crates/ui/src/wcs_gizmo_tests.rs`:** `another_setups_wcs_triad_rides_the_part_into_the_shown_setup` goes through the real `State` commands and the gizmo list. With the mapping disabled it **fails** (\"drawn: [[40, 20, 10]]\"), and it passes with the fix.\n- **`scripts/gate.sh quick`:** all app suites green, including setup_align 9, setup_carry 5 and carried_verify. The ui suites are green except 3 headless-GPU tests (`headless_run_succeeds`, `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`). Those fail with \"No suitable graphics adapter found\" on this host; that is environmental and unrelated to this diff, and the same failure shows up in other PR reviews on this machine.\n- **Named runs:** setup_chip_tests, axis_note_tests and one_wcs all pass.\n- **`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`:** clean.\n- No golden or snapshot changed. Fork synced at v0.15.0.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA by-eye look in the GUI at a two-setup document with a flipped part. Its structure is covered by the gizmo test.\n\nChangelog: Another setup's WCS triad is drawn on its own spot of the part when the shown setup holds the part differently, and is hidden rather than misplaced if the setups can't be related (#558)\n\nFixes #558\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
